  "identifier": "iso-15189",
  "name": "ISO 15189:2022",
  "alternateName": [
    "ISO 15189",
    "Medical laboratories — Requirements for quality and competence"
  ],
  "description": "The international accreditation standard for medical laboratories, defining requirements for quality and competence in clinical testing. Covers personnel competence, equipment validation, method verification, result reporting, and patient data management. Used as the basis for laboratory accreditation by national accreditation bodies (UKAS, DAkkS, RvA, COFRAC, etc.) in over 100 countries. The 2022 revision adds explicit requirements for laboratory information systems (LIS) and digital result reporting, making it directly relevant to teams building clinical laboratory software and AI diagnostics. Paid standard — purchase required from ISO or national body.",
